  "usage_note": "**Assume** in sense 1 is very common in speech: *I assume so* means *I think so, though I have not checked*. **Assuming (that)** at the start of a clause works like **if**: *assuming it doesn't rain, we'll eat outside*.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "She assumed the manager of the team last year.",
      "correct": "She became the manager of the team last year.",
      "note": "In sense 2, **assume** takes a role or a duty as its object (*assume the role of manager*), not a person's title on its own; **became** is simpler."
    }
  ],
